---
description: Always tell the user when an operation or connected set of operations is complete.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Signal completion

After finishing **any** operation or connected set of operations (fix, build, billing wire-up, commit, release, investigation, etc.):

1. **Say clearly that the work is complete** — do not leave the user guessing whether you are still going.
2. State the **outcome in one short line** (what finished / what they can use next).
3. If something is still pending (Stripe keys, upload, user action), say that explicitly; otherwise end on the completion signal.
